1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,120
Exercise 6-5. Liaise the L's. As you work with the following exercise, here are two

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:11,640
points you should keep in mind. When a word ends with an L sound, either A,

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:17,060
connect it to the next word if you can, or B, add a slight schwa for an exaggerated L

4
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:25,960
sound. For example, A, enjoyable as, B, possible. Note, although A is really the

5
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,680
way you want to say it, B is an interim measure to help you put your tongue in the

6
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:34,040
right place. It would sound strange if you were to always add the slight schwa. Once

7
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:37,480
you can feel where you want your tongue to be, hold it there while you continue to

8
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:42,540
make the L sound. You can do the same thing to stop an N from becoming an NG.
